      "logprobs": [],
      "text": "If by “who” you mean a U.S. agency or consultant who can make ChatGPT recommend or mention your company: nobody can legitimately guarantee an organic mention. OpenAI says ChatGPT’s product results are selected independently based on relevance and are not influenced by partnerships or advertising. ([help.openai.com](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11128490-improved-shopping-results-from-chatgpt-search%25252525252525252525252525252525253F.mkv?utm_source=openai))\n\nThere are, however, firms specializing in “GEO,” “AEO,” or AI-search optimization. What they can do is increase the likelihood that ChatGPT can discover, understand, and consider your company—not pay OpenAI to force the model to name it. For an e-commerce company, there’s also a more direct route: OpenAI accepts structured product feeds from approved merchants, and Shopify catalog data is already integrated into ChatGPT. ([developers.openai.com](https://developers.openai.com/commerce/guides/get-started?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you give me your company name and what you sell/do, I can search for U.S.-based agencies that specialize in getting brands surfaced in ChatGPT and compare the strongest candidates."
